GEOPOLITICAL DASHBOARD
======================

A full-screen live dashboard combining a geopolitical map, real-time commodity
prices, live flight radar, and news streams — all served from a single local server.

WHAT'S INCLUDED
---------------
- Interactive world map with Ukraine front line, global data centers, and US military bases
- Live flight radar (US-registered aircraft via ADS-B)
- Real-time commodity prices: Gold, Silver, Copper, Bitcoin, EUR/USD, Oil (via Yahoo Finance)
- Embedded live video streams (Fox News + Yahoo Finance)
- Personal audio stream player with volume and play/pause controls
- Live clock in your local timezone


REQUIREMENTS
------------
- Node.js v18 or newer  (https://nodejs.org)
- npm (comes with Node.js)
- An internet connection (for live prices, flight data, and map tiles)


SETUP
-----

1. Clone the repository

     git clone https://github.com/Luc-Honz/silver-octo-adventure.git
     cd silver-octo-adventure

2. Move into the dashboard folder and install dependencies

     cd dashboard
     npm install

3. Start the server

     node server.js

4. Open your browser and go to

     http://localhost:3002

That's it. The dashboard will open automatically serving all data from the single
local server. No other servers or processes are needed.


USAGE TIPS
----------
- Geo Map:     Use the toggle buttons at the top to show/hide the front line,
               data centers, military bases, and live flights.
               Click any marker or plane dot for details.

- Flights:     Click "Flights" to enable live ADS-B tracking (US aircraft only).
               Dots refresh every 15 seconds.

- Prices:      Commodity prices refresh every 15 seconds from Yahoo Finance.
               Green = up from previous close, Red = down.

- Streams:     Click "Set Stream" on the Fox News or Yahoo Finance panels and
               paste any YouTube live stream URL.

- Audio:       Paste a YouTube URL into the center panel to play audio-only in
               the background. Use the volume slider and play/pause button.


PORTS
-----
Everything runs on a single port:

     http://localhost:3002

No other ports are used.
